    {
      "id": "NAMCOS11",
      "label": "Namco System 11",
      "when": [
        "namco_system11"
      ],
      "input": {
        "name": "PlayStation Arcade Panel",
        "_comment": "A cabinet's panel, per player, and every control ArcadeDuck's boards read: a stick, Start, the coin slot, up to six buttons, a light gun's trigger and reload; a driving cabinet's gear shift, handbrake, view and horn buttons and its music buttons; the select and enter buttons and the sensors of Konami's stranger cabinets - then Service and Test, the two switches behind the coin door (Test opens the board's own menu; a movie that sets the machine up there records it like anything else). Up to four players, because the emulator underneath serves four; which of all this a cabinet HAS is the game's, read from ArcadeDuck's record of it at boot, and the rest is not live. Button 1..6 are the panel's buttons in the order the board wires them - a game names them itself (Tekken: left punch, right punch, left kick, right kick). Gun X and Gun Y are where a light gun is aimed, 0..65535 across the picture and down it. Steering is the wheel, 0 hard left, 65535 hard right, 32768 straight; Accelerator, Brake and Clutch are 0 released and 65535 to the floor. Trackball X and Trackball Y are how far the ball rolled this frame, in the board's own counts.",
